flowchart LR
    A001["<div class='arg'><b>A001 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The Fed's choice at the Sept FOMC is between a hike and risking a large bond spike.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The Fed risks a sharp and disorderly UST long end move.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>P:</b> US 30Y rapidly tests 5.75%.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Bond price action, including post Friday's CPI, shows the bond likes orthodoxy.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> The Fed does not hike with current pricing.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> The Fed faces a simple choice at the Sept FOMC.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]
    A002["<div class='arg'><b>A002 · PREDICTION</b><div class='core pred'><span>The Fed hikes 25bp.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A001 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Friday's CPI data all but lock in a rate hike this week.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Chairman Warsh's Jackson Hole remarks have raised the cost of disappointing expectations significantly.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Current market pricing has raised the cost of disappointing expectations significantly.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Friday's twist flattening of the Treasury curve provides further justification for a hike.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>ALT:</b> The Fed opts to hold in the face of sticky inflation and market pricing.</span><b>[HY]</b></div></div>"]
    A003["<div class='arg'><b>A003 · PREDICTION</b><div class='core pred'><span>Warsh delivers a hawkish hike.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> Warsh in the presser is more Warsh as at Jackson Hole than Warsh as at the July FOMC.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Warsh's Jackson Hole-style presser is largely to support the bond.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> Sept FOMC communications lean hawkish.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> The SEP shows 50bps of total hikes in '26.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>RI:</b> Warsh attempts a #quot;dovish hike#quot; by reassuring markets that the Fed will proceed cautiously.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>RI:</b> Warsh implies few hikes to follow.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> Warsh's hawkish hike supports higher front end rates.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> Warsh's hawkish hike supports twist flattening of the UST curve.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A004["<div class='arg'><b>A004 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The bar for the FOMC to #quot;out-hawk#quot; both expectations as well as other G10 central banks is high.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Part of the puzzle of the dollar being unable to rally amid the recent reacceleration in oil, gas, and refined energy products lies in the broader re-pricing of central banks and curves globally.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>IM:</b> The USD trades more-or-less sideways into year-end (ex-JPY).</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A005["<div class='arg'><b>A005 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The USD outcome is determined by the Fed's ability to #quot;out-hawk#quot; market expectations and other G10 central banks.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A004 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> With evolving expectations, considerable two-way risk remains for the USD at Wednesday's meeting.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]

